WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:09.639
History is full of horrifying events, some
of which are truly more terrifying than any

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:11.620
fictional story.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:19.520
Here's some true stories from History that
will chill you to the bone.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.490
1.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:30.410
The Italian Renaissance was a period in Italy's
history of outstanding art and culture.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:36.930
This 200 year period gave birth to some of
the greatest artists and artworks humanity

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:41.960
has ever known, such as Leonardo Da Vinci
and Michelangelo.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:52.190
But it also gave birth to something considerably
more gruesome, a plague of real life zombies.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:58.100
In 1494 was the first major outbreak of syphilis.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.739
Before antibiotics were invented syphilis
was a fatal infection something to be gravely

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:04.759
feared.

00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:10.909
The disease slowly ate away at the victims
face, causing their flesh to fall away resulting

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:18.850
in the complete destruction of their face
and genitals, within just a few months, and

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:22.920
death would follow shortly afterwards.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.840
During this period it was not uncommon to
see Frenchmen and Italians walking around

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:35.870
with half their face falling off and their
bare skulls exposed, just like a scene from

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:38.079
a horrific zombie movie.

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:40.600
Thank god for modern medicine.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.600
2.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:47.990
Henry Howard Holmes, better known as H.H.
Holmes is widely known as one of America's

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.350
first serial killers.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:56.880
His body count is thought to be somewhere
between 27 and 200.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.880
He achieved this by building a hotel in a
bustling part of Chicago in the 1890s.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:09.550
And designed it to be the perfect killing
arena to fulfil his sick desires.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.290
It later came to be known as "Murder Castle".

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:19.750
H.H. Holmes meticulously designed the hotel
to be a complex maze of windowless rooms.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:26.739
He even hired a handful of different builders
to construct the hotel in sections so only

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:29.010
Holmes would know the layout.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.350
Making escape virtually impossible for his
victims.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:40.150
Every inch of the hotel was designed to confuse
and terrify his victims.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.239
Including doors that only opened from the
outside.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:46.400
Doorways that opened onto brick walls.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:52.900
A safe big enough to put a person inside to
slowly suffocate them.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:59.379
And a chute that allowed Holmes to dump bodies
from the upper floors to the basement, where

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:05.530
two massive furnaces and a large supply of
flesh stripping acid was stored.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.530
3.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:13.340
The Roman city of Pompeii was once one of
the greatest civilisations on Earth, unfortunately

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:19.990
it is most famously known for disaster that
occurred there in 79 AD.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:26.700
When Italy's Mount Vesuvius erupted, wiping
out Pompeii and burying it in ash for over

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.190
a millennium.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:34.519
But even worse effected by the eruption was
Pompeii's neighbouring city Herculaneum.

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:43.240
Just like Pompeii, Herculaneum was also spectacularly
and horrifically buried in volcanic ash.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:49.110
But Herculaneum suffered a fate much worse
than it's more famous neighbour.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:56.629
Herculaneum was also hit by a superheated
pyroclastic flow which is a fast moving current

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:04.840
of hot gas and rock spewed out from a volcano
that reaches speeds of 450 mph.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:11.080
But the most deadly thing about this volcanic
death cloud is that it can reach temperatures

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.629
of up to 1,000 degrees Celsius.

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:20.570
It's incredible speed meant the whole city
would have been engulfed by a 1,000 degree

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.360
cloud of gas in just seconds.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.810
This caused what must have been one of the
most horrific sights in history.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:37.230
The human skull is full of liquids and if
you heat it up super quickly it explodes.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:42.389
This is exactly what happened at Herculaneum
in 79 AD.

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:50.860
The 1,000 degree volcanic cloud caused peoples
skin to vaporise, their brains to boil and

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:57.520
their skulls to literally explode, all in
under a second.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.580
Which sounds like a very good reason not to
live next to an active volcano.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.750
Although this doesn't seem to have got through
to the residents of Naples.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.750
4.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:15.560
During World War II countless atrocities happened
to humans, but animals received their share

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.600
of suffering too.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:23.910
In the 1939, during the run-up to World War
II, the British government formed the National

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.030
Air Raid Precautions Animals Committee.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.430
The purpose of the committee was to decide
what people should do with their pets once

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.050
war broke out.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:40.310
The biggest concern is that food shortages
would be made even worse due to people feeding

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.830
their pets.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:49.850
So to solve the problem the government sent
out pamphlets called "Advice to Animal Owners".

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:56.669
It featured an advertisement for a specific
type of gun, which was best suited to killing

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:03.550
animals and guidelines on how to humanely
dispose of your pet.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:12.210
Within a week of the campaign being launched
750,000 pets across the British isles had

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:18.460
been killed by their owners or taken to purpose
built pet disposal centres.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:22.699
It has come to be known as the Pet Holocaust.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:23.949
5.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:31.100
One of the most horrific stories from all
of history was the Nanking Massacre.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:39.320
During the Second Sino-Japanese War in 1937
the Japanese Imperial Army captured the Chinese

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:43.620
city of Nanking, which was then the Chinese
capital.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:53.410
Over a period of six weeks an estimated 300,000
un-armed Chinese civilians were slaughtered

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.669
by the Imperial Japanese Army.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:07:02.860
But it get's worse, the horrific event is
also widely known as the Rape of Nanking.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:10.419
Because the Japanese forces raped and looted
most of the city's residents before killing

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:11.419
them.

00:07:11.419 --> 00:07:17.740
The Japanese soldiers even raped infants and
the elderly as well as forcing citizens to

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:24.860
commit incestuous acts and many other atrocities
on their fellow Chinese citizens.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:31.050
Ever since the massacre, in attempts to maintain
their pride Japanese officials have outright

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:37.990
denied that the event ever happened, claiming
it was a complete fabrication and an attempt

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:44.550
at anti-Japanese propaganda.

